# GliaKit design system

You are building inside a strict design system. Every visual decision is
already made — your job is to compose, not invent.

## Colors — CSS custom properties only

NEVER hardcode hex values in components. Use semantic tokens via Tailwind:

- Surfaces: `bg-background` (canvas), `bg-card` (raised), `bg-muted` (subtle)
- Text: `text-foreground` (primary), `text-muted-foreground` (secondary)
- Borders: `border-border` — hairlines do the structural work, not shadows
- Brand: `text-primary`, `border-primary` and tints like `bg-primary/10`
  (violet #7C5CFF via token); `text-primary-ink` for brand-coloured text
  and icons that must read on cards. Solid violet fills that carry white text
  (`text-primary-foreground`) use `bg-primary-strong` (#6F4BFF): it passes
  WCAG AA (5.1:1), plain `bg-primary` does not (4.3:1)
- Status: `destructive` (error), `warning` + `warning-foreground`, `diff-add`
  (success) — e.g. `bg-warning/15 text-warning-foreground`. For inline
  notices always use the `Alert` component, never hand-rolled strips
- Signal colors: `var(--signal-violet)`, `var(--signal-cyan)`

The signature violet→cyan gradient (`var(--gradient-signal)`,
`var(--gradient-signal-135)`) is RESERVED for exactly three uses:
1. one hero keyword, 2. primary CTA (gradient Button variant),
3. signal-line dividers / single chart highlight. Never elsewhere.

## Typography

- Headings: `font-heading` (Bricolage Grotesque) + `font-semibold` or `font-bold`, always `tracking-tight`
- Body/UI: default sans (Geist) — never set a font family for body text
- Labels/eyebrows/data: `font-mono` (JetBrains Mono); eyebrows are
  `font-mono text-eyebrow uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-muted-foreground`
- Numbers in tables: `font-mono`

## Components — always reuse, never rebuild

Import from `@/components/ui/*` (docs and live previews for every component
and state: https://www.gliakit.com/components, ordered like the Figma file;
the app screens show them composed in real use):

- **Actions**: Button (variants: default, gradient, outline, secondary, ghost,
  destructive, link · sizes: xs–xl, icon sizes), Chip
- **Forms**: Input + Textarea + Field (label / helper / error) + Label,
  OTPInput, Select, Combobox (searchable), Checkbox (incl. indeterminate),
  Switch, RadioGroup, Slider, DatePicker + Calendar, DateRangePicker,
  FileUpload + FileItem
- **Data display**: Card (default / elevated / outline / media) + CardHeader +
  CardContent + CardFooter + CardMedia + StatCard (delta pill, sparkline,
  `invert` for down-is-good metrics, `tone` tinted / brand / inverse for
  the lead stat), Table/THead/TH/TBody/TR/TD
  (TH takes `sorted` + `onSort`), TableToolbar (search, filters, actions,
  bulk-selection bar), List + ListItem, Badge, Avatar, AreaChart (hover
  tooltip, compare period, `forecastFrom`, `baseline`, `markers`) +
  BarChart (`mode` grouped / stacked / diverging, `series` legend) +
  Sparkline (`kind` line / area / bars) + Rings + ProgressRow — all
  dependency-free, in the `--chart-1…5` palette,
  Accordion
- **Feedback**: Alert (info/success/warning/error), Toast, CircularProgress,
  Spinner, EmptyState
- **Navigation**: Tabs, Breadcrumb + Pagination, Stepper
- **Overlays**: Dialog (size sm / md / lg), Sheet, CommandPalette,
  DropdownMenu, Tooltip

App-level building blocks: `@/components/studio/frames` (AppFrame — the
shell with its composable sidebar, top bar, Columns/Stack/OnTab page
frames and overlays) and `@/components/studio/blocks` (every section as a
typed component: PageHeaderBlock, StatRow, AreaChartCard, BarChartCard,
BreakdownCard, DataTableCard, FilterBarBlock, ScheduleCard, BoardBlock,
TimelineBlock, SettingsFormCard, ToggleListCard …), both generated by
GliaKit Studio. The demo app's shell is `@/components/app/talvo`
(TalvoFrame); AppCommandPalette (⌘K) is mounted in `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`.
The kit's older PageHeader stays in `@/components/app/page-header` for pages
outside the Talvo shell.

If a component is missing, build it in `src/components/ui/` following the
existing patterns (cva variants, data-slot attribute, cn() for classes).

## Layout rules

- Buttons and form controls share `rounded-md` (8px), already built in.
  Only the `xl` marketing Button is a full pill. Badges and Chips are
  `rounded-full`
- Cards and other surfaces (dialogs, lists, table wrappers, panels):
  `rounded-lg border border-border bg-card` (12px, as in Figma)
- Radius scale: `rounded-sm` 6 · `rounded-md` 8 · `rounded-lg` 12 ·
  `rounded-xl` 16 · `rounded-2xl` 20px
- Screens compose inside the `(app)` layout: `PageHeader` first, then
  cards in a `flex flex-col gap-6` (the layout provides it)
- Dark is the default theme; both themes must work — that is free if you
  only use semantic tokens

## Hard rules

- No hardcoded colors, no arbitrary font sizes, no new fonts
- No shadows for structure (borders do that); shadows only for overlays
- No new gradient uses beyond the three sanctioned ones
- Demo data lives in `src/lib/data.ts` — extend it there, not inline
